                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Don'Yoku.  A Japanese arcade pixel art 2 button vertical bullet-hell shooter adorned with a pulse pounding hard rock soundtrack.  No analogue stick support but Xpadder and other 3rd party utilities can remedy this issue.  Store page claims full controller support though you have to enable via options and no native analogue stick support is not full controller support. Controls, both Game-pad and Keyboard are rebind-able.\n\nParaphrasing from in game instructions; Tap A for machine-gun to generate \"DonYoku counter\".  Hold A for beam and release coins from enemies.  More coins the more difficulty as the old green-light page professes.\n\nTwo retro CRT settings. Steam Achievements.   Three difficulty options though the easiest \"Practice\" is a challenge.  Three types of \"aircraft\", spread, narrow and wide shot dispersal.\n\nI really liked Don'Yoku.  Kind of old school arcade, atmosphere, music and sound. A+",
                        "timestamp_created": 1545456803,
